# # SkillAd Project Rules

You are working on the SkillAd production project.

Project Structure:
- admin-panel
- api-server
- landing-page
- mobile-app
- shared-libs

General Rules

1. Read the complete implementation before making changes.
2. Never rewrite working code when a minimal fix is possible.
3. Preserve all existing features unless explicitly instructed.
4. Before editing, identify the root cause of the issue.
5. Modify the minimum number of files required.
6. Never change package versions unless requested.
7. Never change database schema unless requested.
8. Never change API contracts unless requested.
9. Keep compatibility with Expo SDK and Supabase.
10. Preserve the existing UI and UX unless instructed.
11. Reuse existing components whenever possible.
12. Follow the existing project coding style.
13. Explain which files will be modified before making changes.
14. After completing changes, explain how to test them.
15. If uncertain, ask instead of guessing.
16. Never remove features to solve a bug.
17. Avoid unnecessary refactoring.
18. Consider the entire workspace before making cross-project changes.
19. Always prefer production-safe solutions.
20. If a command may be destructive, explain it before suggesting it.